  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Participatory Community-Led Center (PCLC) - Syrbanism (Code 3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Irbin Participatory Community-Led Center (PCLC) is a 15-month pilot that empowers residents of Irbin, a heavily damaged town in Eastern Ghouta, to codesign one of their first shared public spaces after years of siege, displacement, and isolation. The project suggests to transform a destroyed public building &#xa0;into a multifunctional community centre through an inclusive, five-phase process: community consultation, participatory design, rehabilitation, governance training, and activation of the centre. Using Sanoff&#x2019;s style&#xa0;methods such as community mapping, storytelling, children&#x2019;s drawings, and consensus workshops, residents collaboratively shape the center&#x2019;s design and future use. The project strengthens local skills, establishes a community-led governance structure, and reintroduces civic participation in a place where it was long suppressed.</narrative>
  </description>
